## 2026-08-17 03:21 — Iteration 4: explorer/0.5.0 (equip carried gear — operator-flagged)
Operator noticed characters carrying weapons/armor but wearing none. RCA: the
equip action had fired 0 times in all of history — the village SOLD everything
outside KEEP before the equip step could run (buy->sell churn), and looted
armor/shields/trinkets had no equip path at all. Characters fought bare-handed
and UNARMORED, almost certainly compounding the deaths/poison problem.
Fix: equip carried gear into empty slots BEFORE selling; learn each item's slot
by trial (wrong_slot -> try another; stat_requirement -> mark unusable); never
sell gear we can still wear. 83 tests (equip-before-sell / slot-learning /
stat-requirement mutation-checked); reaper gate green. Deployed run #7.
Attribution caveat: shipped ahead of 0.4.0's isolated measurement, so spend_xp
(0.4.0) got only a short window — the next measurement reflects 0.4.0+0.5.0
combined. Prioritized getting characters armored (operator-flagged, survival-
critical) over clean attribution.
Measure next: death rate (deaths/1k ticks, baseline 7.28 on 0.3.0),
status_damage/1k, and a NEW equip-rate metric (% of fielded characters wearing a
weapon and armor, baseline ~0%).

