## 2026-08-20 (iter 25, operator-observed bug) — explorer/0.34.0: urgent survival moves
Trigger: operator watched a wolf attack one of our chars that neither fled nor fought.
Root cause (from data): run #88 had 437 wolf-adjacent char-frames but the char failed
to move 62% of the time (113 low-stamina-stuck). The dodge is a MOVE, and moves need a
1.5x stamina safety margin (0.9.0: raw 20 -> needs 30). A char below the margin (median
stamina-when-adjacent 36, min 6) can't afford to dodge -> RESTS adjacent to the wolf,
taking hits while doing nothing. The margin (meant to stop bounced exploration steps on
stale frames) was starving the ESCAPE move.
Fix: offer() gains `urgent`; survival moves (hurt-retreat, undead-flee + safe-gold grab,
melee-dodge + cornered retreat) offered at RAW cost (no margin) — a bounced step beats
standing to die. Threaded through _retreat. Fixed the SIBLINGS (undead flee, hurt
retreat had the same starvation), not just the wolf case. At stamina 12-29 the char now
escapes; below ~12 (truly exhausted) resting is forced/unavoidable.
Effect/verify: fewer no-op ticks while a predator is adjacent; deaths should ease
further (the KPI alarm + HP-drop diagnostic will confirm on run #90). No wishlist item
this pass (top remaining death-post-mortem ~0.46 < 0.5).

