SUPPORTING MEASUREMENTS made this pass (all from data we already had):
 * XP is SPLIT, two oracles: total xp/kill flat in participant count (5.70 at 1p vs 5.87 at 2p, where
   per-participant predicts 11.40) and a WITHIN-CHARACTER control (16 chars with both solo and shared kills)
   giving a shared/solo ratio of 0.545 vs a split prediction of 0.47. Floor of ~1 xp per participant, so on
   near-worthless mobs (chicken/turtle/sheep) grouping pays slightly MORE in total.
 * The operator corrected my framing — I had measured xp per KILL and treated survival as a footnote. Rate
   measures: DPS on the mob 2.36 -> 4.80 with a second attacker (holds within kind: rat_grey 1.86->6.07,
   wolf 3.78->10.42, skunk 2.59->5.97), party damage intake per tick FLAT (0.51 -> 0.49) because a mob swings
   at one target per tick, so per-MEMBER intake halves (0.51 -> 0.24). ~2x kill speed at ~half personal
   damage = ~4x less damage taken per member per kill. So split xp is NOT an argument against grouping:
   halved share x doubled kill rate leaves xp/time ~unchanged, and buys a large safety margin.
 * METHOD TRAP worth remembering: my first cut compared TIME-TO-KILL by participant count and read backwards
   (TTK ROSE: bat_brown 6->16, mole 10->28). Selection bias — a fight only ACQUIRES a second attacker if it
   lasted long enough for one to arrive, so it measured "long fights attract help", the reverse of the causal
   claim. Rate-based measures are immune; use them whenever the grouping variable is itself time-dependent.
 * PER-WORLD THREAT (400k ticks): vale 4.93 char-deaths/1k frames, dmg/swing 3.91, wildlife -> SPREAD;
   mines 5.06, 4.00, bat/rat/mole+delver/lava_ant -> RAID, and it holds the VEINS; spire 6.64, 5.25, ALL
   undead (vampire_bat/ghoul/cultist/zombie) -> the real frontier, 35% deadlier per frame and we spend 8% as
   much time there as the other two. A MINES RAID IS SIMULTANEOUSLY THE ORE RUN AND THE LEVELLING RUN.
 * DESIGN CONSTRAINT: reactive cohesion cannot work. Median solo TTK is 6 ticks, our mean pairwise distance
   is 22-25 steps, movement is a tile/tick — "gang up, a mob is near" arrives ~16 ticks after the fight
   ended. The coming-together must be STANDING (a leash held while in a dangerous band); only the
   spreading-out half can be reactive.
