PREMISE CHECK 2 — is the cause "too many clubs for bare recruits"? NO. Tracing the buyers: run #117 had 26
buys across 17 distinct chars, with repeat buyers c15386 x6, c15398 x4, c15380 x2. One char bought SIX clubs
at ticks 1397061/67/73/79/85/91 — exactly VILLAGE_ACTION_COOLDOWN (6) apart — and another bought four then
re-equipped the SAME item_id five times. 11 of 31 buys were DUPLICATES within 60 ticks. ~165 gold/run.
So the lever is a BUG FIX, not an economy policy change — much safer and much clearer.
CAUSE: a TIMER is the wrong termination condition for "has my purchase landed?". When the frame is staler
than the cooldown, the char still looks bare when it expires, so the buy re-fires. This is the v0.14.0
re-send storm returning through the same door; bumping the cooldown would only have made it rarer.
FIX: latch the INTENT, clear on OBSERVATION. buy keyed by kind, equip by item_id. Clears on confirmation
(kind in inventory OR already equipped; an equipped item leaves the inventory) or on explicit REJECTION — an
error is as good a termination as a confirmation. INTENT_TTL=60 is only a safety net. `sell` deliberately not
latched (distinct item_ids can't double-spend). The EXISTING equip tests caught v1 immediately: a failed
equip leaves the item in inventory, so the latch blocked the legitimate wrong_slot -> next-slot retry — which
is exactly what the rejection clause is for.
VERIFIED, not asserted: live 0.48.1 = 31 buys / 11 duplicates; candidate over the same frames = 3 buys /
0 duplicates.
