ITER 64 (2026-08-21) — 0.50.0 LEARNED-BLOCK ROOT FIX. Operator asked me to look at our last death; it turned
out to be the same bug as the one before it, and the bug is the dominant death mode returning.
BOTH DEATHS, IDENTICAL SIGNATURE: a hurt char at FULL stamina (56/56), walkable floor beside it, and `rest`
(0.5) as the ONLY weighed option — retreat (8.5) and desperation (8.0) both silent. Recruit-15469 died in the
VALE at tick 1413613 carrying 10 items; Recruit-15484 died in the MINES at 1417806 while burning from a drake
(12 dmg x2 + burn DoT).
CAUSE (bot.py): a tile was learn-blocked whenever a char's position merely LOOKED unchanged after a move.
Frames are stale, so that is NOT evidence of a bounce — and three stale frames in a row seal every exit.
Traced exactly: 15469 moved S at 1413599, E at 1413600, W at 1413601; each looked unlanded, blacklisting
(7,35), (8,36), (6,36) for STUCK_BLOCK_TTL=150 while a crab_green held the fourth side. It then rested TEN
consecutive ticks and bled out. There were ZERO move_failed events and ZERO action errors in either fatal
window — nothing had actually bounced.
This is the v0.42.0 stuck-death returning through the door v0.42.0 did not close: that fix excluded
`not_enough_stamina` specifically, but the NO-ERROR-AT-ALL path still blacklisted.
FIX: the server emits `move_failed` naming the char and the exact tile it could not enter
({"kind":"move_failed","eid":280197,"pos":[5,35],"to":[5,34]}). Blocking is now driven by that event alone;
the position-inference is gone along with the _last_pos/_last_move_dir/_last_move_err bookkeeping that
existed only to qualify it. A stamina rejection emits no move_failed, so v0.42.0's case is handled BY
