Chasing why vein-seek still had not broken a vein found the cause well above ore.

RUN #134 (31,011 frames, and 0.57's bound holding beautifully: move failures 0.5% of moves
against the 5.2% baseline). Vein-seek fired 751 times, all in the mines, streaks averaging
15 ticks — and NO CHARACTER WAS EVER ADJACENT TO A VEIN. Not once. Depth is why: our
characters sat at MEDIAN DEPTH 2 (p90 6) while the shallowest remembered vein is y=26 and
the median is y=88. Only 1.0% of char-frames were within the 14-tile seek range. The seek
was never the problem.

They cannot go deep. POISON_SAFE_DEPTH (v0.23.0) holds an un-healed char above y=12, and
0.0% of char-frames carried a potion_red. BOTH routes to one were shut:
  * BUYING frozen: v0.35.0 raised POTION_RESERVE 100 -> 600 on good evidence (heals were
    99.6% free-brewed, 4511 drinks vs 16 buys; the buy was pinning gold at ~100). Correct
    GIVEN brewing supplies heals. At our real 183 gold, `gold - 20 >= 600` cannot pass.
  * BREWING starved: it needs a `bottle_empty`, and there was NEVER a path to acquire one.
    The kind appeared in exactly two places in the file — KEEP (never sell) and the brew
    gate (count them). Bottles could only ever arrive as loot. Run #134: 0 brews.
So a sound 0.35.0 decision had its premise quietly stop being true, and nothing watched.

0.58.0 fixes the SUPPLY rather than arguing with the reserve. A bottle costs TWO GOLD — the
cheapest unlock anywhere in this chain. Gated on a char that could brew RIGHT NOW if it had
one (_choose_brew must already return a safe batch), so it is provably useful rather than a
standing 2g tax; ordered after arming/armouring and floored at WEAPON_BUY_FLOOR, asserted
end to end rather than by reading the order.

VERIFIED LIVE on #135 (7,940 frames): 2 bottles bought -> 2 brews, against ZERO brews in
the previous 31,011 frames. The pipeline is running again AND it is learning: one brew was
venom-essence (venom_sac+moonbell -> flask_green), the other an UNDECODED LEARNING BATCH
(4x bitterroot -> potion_purple, tells ['sweet_mist']) — new vocabulary from a mechanism
that had been dormant for want of a 2-gold item.

NOT YET CLOSED, and named rather than glossed: still 0.0% potion_red. Neither brewing char
happened to hold a VIGOR batch. embercap is vigor (high confidence) and is carried widely
