iter 74 — 2026-08-21 — trust the server's `overburdened` refusal (0.62.0, run #139)
================================================================================
The v0.61.0 detector's find, fixed. `pickup` confirmed 90 against 811 VIOLATIONS over 20,000
frames of #137, and ALL 1,164 `overburdened` events were the SAME character in the SAME
state: carry (19, 21), two slots free, retrying forever.

A UNITS MISMATCH in a gap neither guard covered. Our fullness test counts SLOTS
(`used >= cap - 1`, needs 20) while the server spends capacity in BULK. At 19/21 a char
cannot take a bulk-3 item, is not "full" by our arithmetic, and is not shedding either (needs
21). It sat between the two and re-issued a doomed pickup nothing learned from — the
pre-0.50.0 learned-block shape again, inferring from the wrong signal.

WHY NOTHING EVER SAW IT: `overburdened` is an EVENT, not an action_error. **The server
refuses through TWO channels and we had only ever watched one.** Every action_error query I
have run on this came back clean while a character burned hundreds of ticks. That
generalises past pickup and is now in the HANDOFF.

FIX: trust the refusal rather than model bulk — ground items do not even expose `bulk` (only
kind/tier), so a bulk model would be inferred and still a guess, while the verdict is a fact.
A refused char reads as full (looting stops) AND sheds (it lightens instead of walking home
under the load). Suppressing pickup alone would have fixed the symptom and left it stuck.
TTL not latch (STUCK_BLOCK's reasoning); scoped to OUR eids, since a rival straining under
its own loot must not stop us looting.

STATED PLAINLY: the defect is BAND-DEPENDENT and currently DORMANT. #137 (rich band) lost
1,164 pickups; #138 (starved) had 103 pickups, 71 successes, ZERO overburdened. The fix will
show its value when loot returns — which is exactly when the defect costs most. Do not expect
a visible delta on a starved run and do not read its absence as failure.

GATE 711 reaper / 703 local; 9 tests, 10 mutants killed.

