That character held TWO ingots. Run #129 had already proven shield_iron needs (3,1), so every
quantity it could afford was known-wrong before it began. It could not know: the knowledge
lives in process memory and dies at every deploy, and we redeploy several times a day.

0.66.0: proven recipes persist (new `learned` table), hydrated once per process; and once a
product has a proven quantity that is the ONLY one sent — unaffordable means "not on today's
menu", not "walk the ladder again". Discovery untouched: an unproven product still walks the
whole ladder.
ONLY POSITIVE FACTS ARE STORED. `wrong_materials` is not deterministic in what we key on, so
a persisted failure would carry a wrong belief into every future run — the v0.55.0 mistake
(remembered chest CONTENTS driving targets) in a new place. Failures stay per-run, cheap and
self-correcting.
