frames. So `bot._forged` stayed empty, `recently_forged` was always False, and v0.64.0's
proof-outranks-refusal rule NEVER RAN LIVE, across two versions.
This REPLACES the softer story in the retraction above. I said 0.64.0 was "structurally right
but bought no measured gain". The truth: it was INERT, so the corrected series
(33%/26%/21%/17%) contains no information about it either way. And 0.66.0's persistence was
built on a proof path that could never produce a proof.
0.66.1 parses events for EVERY frame in one place; a test pins that the field side survived
the move.

THE PART THAT GENERALISES: the whole suite passed before AND after. 752 tests and not one
asserted that a village frame's events are read — every test of the proof rule drove the
strategy or the monitor directly, never the ROUTING between them. The chain was broken in the
MIDDLE, where both ends test clean. There is now an end-to-end test walking a forge attempt
through a village frame to a proven recipe to a persisted row, mutation-killed at every link.
THIRD INERT SHIPMENT (0.48 misread as inert but wasn't; 0.54 genuinely inert; 0.64 now), and
all three shared one shape: CODE THAT WAS CORRECT AND NEVER REACHED. Green tests measure the
code you call, not the code the bot runs. When a fix shows no effect, FIRST ask whether it
executed — before interpreting the numbers at all.

