iter 81 — 2026-08-22 — a character that never walks home never learns (0.68.0, run #147)
================================================================================
v0.67.0 raised INT exactly ZERO times on run #146, and the cause was upstream of everything
it did: THE TOME HOLDER NEVER WENT TO THE VILLAGE. `tome_field` sat in c16041's pack for all
10,933 of its tome-carrying frames, every one in vale (village share 0.4%). The learn step
lived only in `village()`, so it never learned — and never earned the `stat_requirement`
refusal that 0.67.0's INT investment keys on. The whole chain was waiting on an event that
could not occur.

0.68.0 offers the learn in the FIELD. `use` is not a village verb — it is already how potions
are drunk out there. Scored 3.0: below adjacent harvest (3.3) and everything urgent, above
the frontier push (2.5), inside the safe non-homing branch, so a hurt character does not stop
to read (tested).
VERIFIED LIVE within minutes on #147: 2 learn decisions -> 2 `use` actions -> 2
`stat_requirement` refusals. The refusal is now EARNED, which is the input 0.67.0 was missing.
And the holder does reach the village occasionally (11% of its frames on #147), so the XP
spend that follows is reachable. Chain should now close without further changes — watching
rather than building.

*** FOURTH TIME A LINK WAS CORRECT AND UNREACHABLE. THIS IS THE PATTERN OF THE PROJECT. ***
  v0.54.0 vein-seek   — validated against a map the PROCESS did not have
  v0.64.0 proof rule  — events parsed only on frames it never saw
  v0.67.0 INT buy     — keyed on state that dies at deploy
  v0.68.0 learn step  — running in a place the character never goes
Always the same shape: code that executes somewhere the subject is not. "It is implemented"
is no longer an acceptable answer to "why is nothing happening" — the questions are WHERE does
this run, and FOR WHOM. Before shipping a behaviour, name the frame it fires on and the
character it fires for, and check that character actually gets there.

NOT FIXED, written down instead: `_tome_failed` is still in-memory and dies at every deploy —
the OTHER reason 0.67.0 was inert on #146. The field offer makes a refusal cheap to re-earn,
