0.76.0 — THE ORDERING WAS THE BUG. v0.69.0 set POTION_RESERVE equal to WEAPON_BUY_FLOOR so
the heal would "rank WITH arming". The arithmetic made it strictly worse: the weapon fires
at gold > 150 while _afford_potion needs gold - 20 >= 150, i.e. 170 — the heal was HARDER
to afford than the weapon AND checked after it. With a bare bench there is always someone
to arm, so the surplus went at 151 every time. #157: 0 bought, 0 brewed, gold at 149. One
coin under the floor that unlocks the map. Heal now checked FIRST, floor 100 (below the arm
floor). Bounded by POTION_KEEP=1, and a test proves a HEALED char then gets armed.
EARLY (5.3k frames): 4 potion buys, no errors, healed share 0.5% -> 2.7%, gold 102.
FALSIFICATION stated before deploy: buys > 0, healed share >> 0.5%, median fielded y > 0,
looted-out share falling from 31%. If buys happen and y does not move, the cap was not the
only pin.

