================================================================================
LEDGER CAUGHT ITS FIRST REAL BUG — in the measuring instrument itself. recheck_claims
reported "run #149 sale-gold CONTRADICTED, recomputed 0.0" against data that had not
changed, on one CLI run in three. Root cause: attribution.our_guild_id() read the NEWEST
decision row's char_uid, but guild-level decisions (recruit/embark, 476k rows) carry NULL —
so whenever the live bot's last write was one, the ownership filter went blind and every
sale was dropped. A FLAKY oracle is worse than a wrong one: it cries wolf exactly as often
as the village loop acts. Fix: WHERE char_uid IS NOT NULL. Mutation-checked; 5 consecutive
clean CLI runs. (The recheck path was fine — three-valued verdicts worked as designed; the
oracle underneath it raced the write head.)

