ITER 84 (2026-08-24, explorer/0.102.0): WIZARD RECALL HYSTERESIS (operator: "ship the
hysteresis fix" for the return-home loop). Diagnosed #194's return spam (2711 returns/17k
ticks): the ARCH-WIZARD (INT 8, our magic hope) oscillated home 222x — the single biggest
returner. Cause = OBSERVATION STALENESS: a wizard only knows a world is dangerous WHILE in
it; back home that knowledge expires (THREAT_TTL), so the embark check reads the world
"safe" and re-dispatches it into the same bad band the field just pulled it from. The
band-gate (0.87.1, sit out dangerous bands) and pair-embark (0.87.0, send it out) are both
intentional but UNCOORDINATED -> thrash. FIX: after a band-danger fallback, stamp
self._wizard_recall[uid]=tick; the embark skips a wizard whose recall is younger than
WIZARD_RECALL_COOLDOWN=200 ticks (~a band cycle; band_refresh_deferred carries in_ticks
120) -> the wizard WAITS OUT the band at home instead of bouncing. 5 tests (waits /
re-embarks-after / no-recall-embarks / pinned / end-to-end-stamp); 3/3 mutants killed
after adding the end-to-end test (the unit tests stamped manually, masking the stamp
mutant). Should sharply cut the 2711 returns AND stop wasting the arch-wizard's time so it
can STAY OUT and level toward the tome. NEXT: measure #195 — returns/1k down? arch-wizard
stint length up? (still the brewing/gold lever owed for the tome itself.)

ITER 85 (2026-08-24, explorer/0.103.0): THE LINE DANCE — un-healed chars oscillating at
the poison-safe-depth boundary (operator: "it looks like the guild is line dancing
again"). Traced c19457 on run #195 flip-flopping N/S/N/S at y12/13 (POISON_SAFE_DEPTH=12),
hp 36/36 healthy, UNHEALED (no potion_red). MECHANISM: the gather block (gold/chest/loot
beelines, 5.0/4.5/4.0) was gated ONLY on `not homing` — no depth check. The retreat block
turns an un-healed char home from y>=cap at 2.5 ("no heal past the safe depth"). So loot
one tile past the cap (N, 4.0) OUT-SCORED the home-retreat (S, 2.5): step N past the cap,
retreat turns it back S, loot reappears N, forever. A two-attractor boundary thrash with a
stamina-rest gate between steps. FIX (bot-side, hoisted has_heal + a `deep_ok(step)`
guard): a gather STEP is suppressed when it would carry an un-healed char past
POISON_SAFE_DEPTH — the SAME threshold the retreat already uses, so the two rules agree
about the cap instead of fighting over it. At the boundary the deeper loot pull vanishes
and the char commits home; loot within the cap is still pursued. Applied to all three
gather steps (gold/chest/loot). 2 tests in test_decision_engine.py, both mutation-checked
from OPPOSITE sides: line-dance test fails when the guard is neutralised (allow-all
mutant, char chases loot N); over-suppression test fails when the guard denies-all (char
won't gather in-cap loot E). Together they pin `has_heal or step[1] <= POISON_SAFE_DEPTH`
exactly. 1096 local/reaper green. NEXT: measure #196 — un-healed-char oscillation (rapid
dir reversals at a fixed pos) down? no loss of shallow gather income? (still the
brewing/gold lever owed for the tome, and #195's wizard-recall returns/1k measurement.)

